Brigand wrote on 11 Aug 2005 10:45:20 -0700:
> Why is a ranger considered hard to ascend?? 

For starters, they get one less HP per levelup than other classes do.  
More importantly, their starting stats are quite inferior to those of the 
S,V,B, etc.  The two important stats are STR, for more damage and to-hit, 
and CON, for more HP per levelup.  And both stats improve carrying 
capacity.

From stat-343.txt:
  
Player Class     STR      INT      WIS      DEX      CON      CHA     REM
~~~~~~~~~~~~    ~~~~~    ~~~~~    ~~~~~    ~~~~~    ~~~~~    ~~~~~    ~~~
Barbarian       16-30     7- 6     7- 7    15-20    16-30     6- 7      8
Ranger          13-30    13-10    13-10     9-20    13-20     7-10      7

One needs at least 15 CON to get any HP bonus at all; over half of rangers 
will not have this and so get only d6+d2 (a human ranger, of course) HP 
per levelup, which averages 5 HP.  

Meanwhile 70% of barbarians have 18 CON.  If human, they gain d10+d2+4 HP 
per levelup, which averages 11 HP.

You can do similar calculations for STR to show the barbarian doing way 
more damage.  The best feature of the ranger class is the cloak of 
displacement, and it just isn't good enough to make up for the 
disadvantages.


